<Placemark>   <name>Deiwelselter</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Burial Chamber or Dolmen <b>Alt Name:</b> Autel du Diable, Devil's Altar <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>3</b> Condition: <b>2</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>3</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 49.8582 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 6.1525<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/benelux/luxembourg/thumb/450px-Luxembourg_Diekirch_Deiwelselter_01.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    The seven metre tall Deiwelselter, or Devil's Altar, was re-built in 1892 with stones of a former dolmen. A recent research dated dated the dolmen about 2,000 BCE.
. Access: 2km south-west of Diekirc...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=12842" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#6_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>6.1525,49.8582,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
